\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces CO$_2$ + H$_2$O phase equilibria at six representative temperatures ($25$--$250\,^\circ $C). For each temperature, the left panel shows the CO$_2$ mole fraction in the aqueous phase ($x_{\text  {CO}_2}$) and the right panel shows the H$_2$O mole fraction in the CO$_2$-rich phase ($y_{\text  {H}_2\text  {O}}$) vs.\ pressure. Open symbols: experimental data \citep  {Coelho2025}; black solid line: CPA (salt-free); rainbow-colored filled bands: eCPA predictions spanning NaCl molalities $m_s = 0$--$6$\,mol\,kg$^{-1}$ (filled between consecutive molality contours; violet $\approx 0$, red $= 6$\,mol\,kg$^{-1}$), with discrete eCPA curves overlaid. Results for all 35 temperatures are shown in Fig.~\ref {fig:co2h2o_Tpanel_SI}.}}{13}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
